P1 — HM-TRADES-RECENT-CONSOLIDATE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Per audit: 6 distinct callers of /api/trades/recent hit on a 
single Bridge load with different params. None are strict 
duplicates but all are consolidatable.

Callers identified:
  line 12595 — fetchCapitolPortfolio       player=capitol&limit=50
  line 16172 — arena leaderboard row       player={pid}&limit=5&season=cur
  line 16585 — fetchArenaFeed              limit=30&season=cur
  line 16955 — toggleSidebarAgent          player={pid}&limit=8&season=5
  line 18504 — checkNewTrades              limit=5
  line 26021 — pollShipComputerAlerts      limit=20

PROPOSED PATTERN — shared in-memory store:

  // Module-level cache + fetcher
  const _tradesRecentStore = {
    data: null,
    timestamp: 0,
    TTL_MS: 30000,  // 30s
    inflight: null
  };
  
  async function getTradesRecent({player_id=null, limit=50, season=null} = {}) {
    const now = Date.now();
    
    // Stale-while-revalidate: return cache if fresh
    if (_tradesRecentStore.data && (now - _tradesRecentStore.timestamp) < _tradesRecentStore.TTL_MS) {
      return _filterTrades(_tradesRecentStore.data, {player_id, limit, season});
    }
    
    // Coalesce in-flight requests
    if (_tradesRecentStore.inflight) {
      return _tradesRecentStore.inflight.then(d => _filterTrades(d, {player_id, limit, season}));
    }
    
    // Fetch broadest scope (limit=100, no filters) — let client filter
    _tradesRecentStore.inflight = fetch('/api/trades/recent?limit=100')
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(d => {
        _tradesRecentStore.data = d;
        _tradesRecentStore.timestamp = Date.now();
        _tradesRecentStore.inflight = null;
        return d;
      })
      .catch(e => {
        _tradesRecentStore.inflight = null;
        throw e;
      });
    
    return _tradesRecentStore.inflight.then(d => _filterTrades(d, {player_id, limit, season}));
  }
  
  function _filterTrades(data, {player_id, limit, season}) {
    let trades = data.trades || data;
    if (player_id) trades = trades.filter(t => t.player_id === player_id);
    if (season) trades = trades.filter(t => t.season === season);
    if (limit) trades = trades.slice(0, limit);
    return {trades};
  }

REPLACE 6 callers with getTradesRecent() calls. Each caller becomes:
  // Before: await fetch('/api/trades/recent?player_id=capitol-trades&limit=50')
  // After:  await getTradesRecent({player_id: 'capitol-trades', limit: 50})

PERF EXPECTATION
  Before: 6 fetches per Bridge load
  After: 1 fetch + 5 cache hits
  Win: -83% trades/recent fanout
  Steady state (30s TTL): all callers <1ms

VERIFY
  # Open browser DevTools Network tab, hard-refresh Bridge
  # Filter to /api/trades/recent
  # Count: should be 1, was 6

GUARDRAILS
- limit=100 default may miss historical lookups — verify each 
  caller's max needed limit; bump default if any caller needs >100
- If season filter matters semantically (Season 6 vs all-time), 
  preserve in _filterTrades; don't drop the filter
- DO NOT change /api/trades/recent backend — pure frontend dedupe

